From 1683198693e46a0fb5394a76aa05a1959477ba42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 14:34:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make the layout work on phones and tablets
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Measured across 320-1024px. The page never scrolled sideways, but several
things were unusable on touch:

- Panels and the light desk scrolled inside themselves, so the page had
  nested scroll regions on touch. Inner scrolling is now desktop-only; on
  small screens panels grow and the page scrolls.
- Queue reordering was impossible: HTML5 drag doesn't fire on touch. Small
  screens now get move buttons; the drag handle stays on desktop.
- The queue's remove button only appeared on hover, so it was invisible on
  touch.
- Faders were 26px tall and segmented buttons 27px. A pointer:coarse block
  now sizes faders, switches, segments and buttons for fingers. It lives at
  the end of the stylesheet — placed earlier, the base rules outranked it.
- Grid items default to min-width:auto, so nowrap content pushed panels up
  to 337px inside a 288px track at 320px wide. Panels and segment buttons
  can now shrink.
- The stage header collided with the control panel button, and hero text sat
  unreadable over the bright rig. Header scales down, and gradient scrims
  sit behind the text.
- The rig was laid out for landscape: fixture apertures, pools and the booth
  scaled off raw height, so they ballooned on tall screens. Hardware now
  scales off min(h, w*0.62) and the arch fits the width.
- The admin page overflowed 165px on a phone; track rows wrap their actions
  and form fields stack.

Adds scripts/e2e-mobile.mjs covering the touch paths the desktop suite
cannot reach.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018JjAD7WNZmP26cnkvFDZws
